        <head>PROVISION FOR RRSHRVR FOND.</head>
        <p>PROVISION FOR RRSHRVR FOND.</p>
        <p>After providing for Preference dividends, it is intended each year—until the General Reserve Fund amounts to £lo,Oo—to add at least 10 per cent. of the *Mance of avail- able profits to the General Reserve Fund before paying any dividend for that year on the Ordinary Shares. DIVIDEND GUARANTEED BY BOOT'S PURE DRUG CO., LTD. FOR TEN YEARS.</p>
        <p>Boot's Pure Drug Co., Ltd. (one of the Vendors, and holder of all the Ordinary shares of the other Vendor Company. viz., Boots, Cash Chemists (Western), Limited, has entered into a covenant with Trustees on behalf of the holders of the shares now offered for the purpose of guaranteeing a divi- dend ofj six per eent, per annum upon such shares until the 30th June, 1909.</p>
        <p>RIGHT OF RBDIIMPTION EY BOOT'S PURE DRUG CO.,</p>
        <p>LTD.. AT 6s. PER SHARE FERMIUM.</p>
        <p>In consideration of this guarantee Boot's Pure Drug Co. Ltd., reserves the right to purchase all or any of these shares at any time after the 33th June, 19)4, on giving three months' prior notice, at not less than 265. per share, and the share certificates will be endorsed with this proviso.</p>
        <p>DIRECTORS. ALD. JAMES DUCKWORTH, .1.P., Castlefield, Rochdale W. B. THORPE (Director, Nottingham. Joint Stock Bank),</p>
        <p>Lenton House. Nottingham JESSE BOOT, btation-street, Nottingham (Managing Director). TRUSTEE FOR GUARANTEED SHAREHOLDERS. ALDERMAN JAMES DUOKWORTH„ M.P., Castlefleld, Rochdale. ALDEEMAN JOSEPH TOMPSON, Riversdale, Wilmslow Park, Manchester.</p>
        <p>SOLICITORS. WELLS AND HIND, Nottingham. BANKERS.</p>
        <p>NATIONAL PROVINCIAL BANK OF ENGLAND, LTD., Manchester. Liverpool. Birmingham and Branchcs. NOTTINGHAM JOINT STOCK BANK LTD., Victoria Street, Nottingham, and Branches. AUDITORS.</p>
        <p>SHARP, PARSONS AND (Chartered Accountants), London and Birmingham. REGISTERED OFFICE, STATION STRRKT. NOTTINGHAM.</p>
        <p>BOOTS, CASH CHEMISTS (LAsIZA.SIIIRE), LIMITED, has been formed for the purpose of acquiring twenty-eight saleshops and premises of Boots (Cash Cusmists (Western). Limited, and seven saleshops and premises of Boot's Pure Drug Co., Limited, and of taking over the business of Retail Chemists and Druggists now carried on by the Vendor Companies upon such premises, together with the stook, fixtures, and fittings, and of extending the said business.</p>
        <p>The said salesh-ops and premises, with the exception of two held upon annual tenancies. re either freehold or held under leases of terms varying from forty-six years downwards. and are situate as follows :</p>
        <p>MANCHESTER. 17-19. St. Ann St., St. Ann's LIVERPOOL. eq. 93, Bold Street 48-se, Oldham Street 11-13, London Road 105, Market Street I. Lena Street 1, Oxtord Street 111, County Road. Walton 11-13, Stretford Road 203, Scotland Road 43, Downing Street 14. West Derby Road 83, Alexandra Road, Moss 420, Stanley Road Sias 235, Park Road 91, Regent Road, Salford ' BIRKENHEAD. 617, Stockport Road, Long- 239, Grange Road eight WARR'NGTON. ECCLES. • 5. Bridge Street 58. Church street • 35. Bridge Street __ . _</p>
        <p>STOCXPORT.</p>
        <p>Market *date</p>
        <p>26, Bridge Street Brow SOUTHPORT. ALTRINCRINI. ' 199-201, Lord Street 37, Railway Street ST. HELENS. LEIGH. 6,Ormskirk Street 3-5, Railway Road WIGAN. GLOSSOP. 47-49, Waligate 19, High Street, W PRESTON. DAMIEN. 27. Fishergate</p>
        <p>10, Market Street BEACKPOoL. ACCRINGTON. 14, Market Street 17, Post Offica Arcade DOUGLAS (1.0. M. LANCASTER. 22, Duke Street 45-47, Penny Street All the above premises have been specially adapted and fitted up for the trade now carried on therein. Some have been:entirely reconstructed, and others completely rebuilt, either by, or for the vendor Companies. The freeholds and most of the leaseholds are situated in commanding positions on the leading thoroughfares of large towns, and in every case the very best business situations available have been acquired. The fittings of the shops are of a most attractive character, and, as material of an endur- ing nature has been used throughout, the expense oo re- newals and repairs will be reduced to a minimum. No other firm has had such an extensive experience in adapting premises structurally to the special requivments of chemists as the vendor Companies. Add to this the convenience of the general appointments of the various departments, such as, dispensing, &amp;a., the expensive and enduring quality of the fittings, the complete stocks of chemists' and druggists' goods of the freshest and best qualities, and the property acquired forms a group of saleshops far surpassing even the best of the ordinary chemists' shops. beveral of the shops are already old-established and thriving branches with a good and profitable trade. All the others have prosperous businesses with a good and improving trade in their respective localities with the exception of some half-a-dozen which are in process of developing a growing connection, and of two which were in preparation for opening at the date from which the Company takes over the business. Negotiations are at present proceeding for leases of other shops on leading thoeoughfares in Manchester. The value of the premises acquired by the Company may be best judged from the fact that (exclusive ot stock) the Bold-street and London-road prennises in Liverpool aost older £ll,OOO. Every Branch is under the management of a Chemist fully qualified by examination of the Pharmaceutical Society. The Company will take over the assets and businesses as from the 31st March, 1899. APPLICATION FORMS for SHARES and FULL PROS- PECTUS with views of some of the leading branches may be obtained at 5, BRIDGE STREET, 35, BEIDGE STREET, MARKET GATE. or NATIO NI AL PaOVINCIAL BANK of ENGLAND, LIMITED, WARRINGTON, or the following form may be used :</p>
        <p>July 1899. This form must be sent entire to the Office of the Com- pany. Station Street, Nottingham ; or to the National Provincial Bank of England, Manchester, Liverpool, Bir- mingham, and Branches ; or to the Nottingh,tm Joint Stock Bank, Lta.. Victoria Street, Nottingham. FORM OF APPLICATION FOR SHARES.</p>
        <p>BOOTS, CASH CHOMISTi (LANCASHIRE), LIMITED.</p>
