      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-07-07_WidnesExaminer_art0072" n="art0072">
        <head>WARRINGTON.</head>
        <p>WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>PROSPECTUS.</p>
        <p>Messrs. Boots, Cash Chemists (Lancashire), Limi- ted, are now offering for public subscription 55,000 six per cent. guarantee, .E 1 preference shares. The dividends have been guaranteed for 10 years by goon Pura Drug C3mpany, Limited, and in con- sideration of this guarantee, the company just men- tioned reserves the right to purchase all or any of these shares at any rime after the 30th June, 1904 on giving three months prior notice, at not les, than 26s per share. The company has been formed for the purposes of acquiring twenty-eight saleshops and premises, of Boots, Cash Chemie's (Western), Limited, and seven saleshops and premises of Boots Pure Drug Company, Limited and of taking over tUe business of retail chemists and druggists now being carried on by the vender companies. The shops are situeted in Manchester, Liverpool and the principal c•,mtres of population in Lancashire and Cheshir:e Tiiree very successful establishments of this firm are, of course, situated in Warrington, and the business aptitude shown here is typical of that displayed by the compeny wherever branches are formed. The auditors' re- port shows that the preference dividends are now being fully earned, and it is confidently expected that within five years at the furthest the business will have become sufficiently remunerative to pay a substantial dividend on the ordinary shares, but, meanwhile, to make the preference shareholders' dividends safe from the start, and to ensure their punctual payment throughout, irrespective of the first year's trading profits, Boot's Pure Drug Com- pany, Limited, as already stated, guarantees them for ten years. The shares are offered for subt•crip- tion at 21s. each, the is. per share premium being carried to a general reserve fund, and the Company will thus start with a reserve fund of £3,400. The dividends will be paid quarterly, the first dividend being payable on the 30th September, next. Ap- plication forms for shares may be obtained at the local branches of the company or at the National Provincial &amp;ink of England, Limited, Bridge- street.</p>
