        <p>WEEKLY REPORT ON THE HEALTH OF WARRINGTON. Week Ending Saturday 24th June, 1899. During the week the following births and deaths were registered : Births. Deaths. Warrington Registration District 36 36 The excess of births over deaths was nil. The Birth Rate was equal to 293 per 1,000. The death-rate from all causes was equal to 293 per 1,000, against 17.8 the average, of the previous 4 weeks, and against 13.2 the corresponding period of last year. The death- rate from the seven chief zymotic diseases was equal to 8.9 per 1,000. against 4.4 the average rate of the previous 4 weeks, and against 0.8 the corresponding period of 1898. The aces of mortality were- -0-1 1-5 5-15 15-25 25-65 65 ap. 10 12 10 4 36 The deaths included-1 from scarlet fever, 1 from diphtheria. 7 from measles, 1 from whoop:ng cough, 1 from diarrhcea, 2 from phth!sis, 3 frcm lung diseases, 1 from heart disease, 19 from all other causes. The following cases of Infectious Disease have been reported during the week :—Scarlet fever 10 cases, diphtheria 1 case, erysipelas 1 6se. Total number of patients in hospital week ending 24th June, 48. METEOROLOGY—The mean temperature was 59 Fah., and therefore the same as th previous week. The maximum temperature 75F., was recorded on the 21,t inst., and the minimum temperature 43F., on the 19. h inst. The Rainfall measured 'BB inch. The general direc- tion was SE. JOHN H. GORNALL, Medical Officer of Health.</p>
